<title>ITALY: Milan airports April cargo traffic up 5.4pct.</title>
<headline>Milan airports April cargo traffic up 5.4pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by Milan's airport system in April increased by 5.4 percent against the same period 1996,the airport authority said. This increase reflects Alitalia's moving all cargo flights from to Turin-Caselle to Milan Malpensa.</p>
<p>					Total Milan System</p>
<p>			   April	Pct	   Jan/Apr    Pct</p>
<p>			   1997	 Change	1997	 Change</p>
<p>Cargo (Tonnes)	 14,804    up 20.3	 58,454    up  5.4</p>
<p>Mail (Tonnes)	   1,179    up.29.1	  4,385    up 13.5</p>
<p>Passengers	  1,551,016    up 15.3    5,481,215    up 12.7</p>
<p>Aircraft Moves	 16,784    up  5.4	 63,897    up  6.8</p>
<p>LINATE</p>
<p>			  April	Pct	   Jan/Apr    Pct</p>
<p>			  1997	 Change	1997	 Change</p>
<p>Cargo (Tonnes)	  5,181  down  3.7	 20,803  down  4.2</p>
<p>Mail (Tonnes)	   1,155    up 29.4	  4,280    up 13.7</p>
<p>Passengers	  1,257,538    up 19.3    4,294,788    up 14.7</p>
<p>Aircraft Moves	 13,909    up  6.7	 52,323    up  7.0</p>
<p>MALPENSA</p>
<p>			  April    Pct	    Jan/Apr    Pct</p>
<p>			  1997     Change	 1997	 Change</p>
<p>Cargo (Tonnes)	 9,623    up 38.9	  37,651    up 11.5</p>
<p>Mail (Tonnes)	     24    up 18.4	     105    up  6.5</p>
<p>Passengers	   293,478    up  0.5     1,186,427    up  6.0</p>
<p>Aircraft Moves	 2,875  down  o.4	  11,574    up  5.9</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
